comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-26T14:54:31.384Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-09-26: searched all statuses for listAllComplete, legacy alias migration hints, and canonical read receipt. pm-y4aaol is the closed whole-list implementation parent; pm-0z7n is the closed alias foundation; no item tracks this published SDK regression. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1315."
  "2026-09-26T14:59:47.699Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: the public SDK integration test failed before the fix with legacy_aliases_used=[--full,--no-truncate] on listAllComplete(). The same test passes after marking the helper-generated options and preserving provenance through runtime normalization. Explicit SDK aliases remain reported, and the CLI recovery still reports its explicit --no-truncate alias."
  "2026-09-26T15:04:28.909Z","harness:codex","Manual installed acceptance: packed this branch, installed into separate temporary npm and Bun projects, exercised npx and bunx init/create/version, and called published SDK listAllComplete(). Both returned one certified row and zero legacy aliases. The SDK import-cost gate passed after moving provenance to a lightweight module."
  "2026-09-26T15:43:46.218Z","harness:codex","Verification: linked sandboxed SDK integration passed 3/3, complete-list unit plus CI directory contracts passed 51/51, TypeScript and ESLint passed, focused exact coverage covers the skill generator 100/100/100/100, installed npm/npx and Bun/bunx temp projects returned a certified one-item corpus with no false aliases, local SDK import-cost gate passed, graph-composition and record-integrity assurance passed, and bounded mutation gate scored 323 killed/7 equivalent. The full local suite first found two structural test failures, both corrected and focused reverified; final exact full coverage remains for required PR CI. Local CLI transport timing missed tight limits, and unchanged main also missed create by 5ms on this host; no timing baseline was weakened."
